  "elevationPhilosophy": "Depth is almost entirely flat. The single shadow in the system is a 1px/5% lift on cards — it exists only to break a card from the canvas when a border alone isn't enough. Borders do the heavy lifting; shadows are a last resort.",
  "imagery": "Common is essentially imageless — the visual identity is carried by the aurora gradient on the launch card and the two filled token dots, not by photography or illustration. Where icons appear (magnifier, theme toggle, help, close, arrow), they are 16px line icons with 1.5px stroke weight in Carbon or Ash, sitting inside 1px-bordered 6px-radius containers. Token entries are represented by the two-color dot pair (Cobalt + Ultraviolet, 8px each) — no avatars, no thumbnails, no product imagery. The only gradient treatment that functions as 'imagery' is the aurora wash and the spectrum button, both of which are system elements, not decorative media. There are no people, no product photos, no screenshots anywhere in the interface.",
  "layout": "The page is a max-width 1200px centered column on a white canvas, with a thin side rail on the left (≈200px, whitespace-separated, not bordered) and the main content column on the right. The hero is a full-width launch card with the aurora gradient, sitting flush between the top nav and the first list section. Below the hero, content is a single vertical stack of section header rows (Trending, Recently Launched, Graduated, Trending Communities) each followed by a list — no multi-column grids, no card carousels, no masonry. Navigation is a top bar with a borderless full-width search, right-aligned controls, and a compact notification strip above it. The layout rhythm is: gradient card → repeated plain rows → repeated plain rows. The eye is led by the gradient, then by the alignment of section labels and right-aligned arrow links. Density is compact — 8–16px element gaps, 32px section gaps, no hero illustration to compete with the launch card.",
  "customSections": [
    {
      "title": "Agent Prompt Guide",
      "content": "$1e"
    },
    {
      "title": "Color Rationing Rules",
      "content": "The system is monochrome by default. Color is a resource, not a baseline.\n- **Carbon & Paper** handle all structural and textural work (text, hairlines, fills, surfaces).\n- **Silver, Mist, Ash, Obsidian** form the neutral scale — borders get lighter as emphasis drops, from #000000 structural lines down to #e0dfe1 input edges.\n- **Cobalt and Ultraviolet** appear only as 1px strokes, 8px filled dots, and link text. They never fill large surfaces.\n- **The spectrum gradient** (cobalt→violet→ember) is the system's only high-chroma fill. It appears in exactly two places: the aurora launch card surface and the spectrum launch button. No other element may use it.\n- **The aurora wash** (30% opacity) is the soft form of the spectrum — used only for the launch card and the notification banner background."
